@import com.aiforum.web.ActivityRow
@import com.aiforum.web.FeedCards
@param events: List<ActivityRow>

<%-- The activity stream: every thread opening and every settled comment as its own card, newest first
     across both, each linking INTO its thread at that event (a post card's event id IS its thread id, so
     it lands on the opening post's existing #reply-<threadId> anchor).

     TWO DESTINATIONS, and which is which is the whole point: the box opens this event at its anchor
     (activity-card__open, stretched across the card by app.css BEHIND the content), and the thread
     TITLE opens the conversation at its top.

     THE EXCERPT IS A PLAIN <span>, DELIBERATELY. It was an <a> for exactly one commit, so that clicking
     the words navigated too — and the owner reported that its text could then not be selected with the
     mouse. Dragging from inside a link drags the LINK; draggable="false" is the documented cure and it
     did not deliver here. Rather than ship a third guess at someone else's browser, the text stopped
     being a link: plain text in a span selects the way all other text on the page does, with nothing to
     verify. The cost is stated where it will be found — clicking the WORDS does nothing; clicking
     anywhere else in the card opens the event.

     The empty <a> is the click target, and it is a real focusable link rather than a decorative
     overlay, so the comment stays reachable by keyboard (the title link only reaches the thread). Its
     aria-label is a fixed string on purpose: the thread title is prose, and prose in an ATTRIBUTE is
     the one thing this page never does (JTE does not escape ">" there — §2.5, I2).

     NOTE the box link exists at all because nav.js used to eat this click: it saw [data-nav-item] and
     moved its reading cursor instead of navigating. That half is fixed in nav.js.

     The hook vocabulary here is DISJOINT from the thread card's (I1): no data-thread-*, no delete
     control. That is what lets "the activity view shows no thread cards" be a property — a scan for the
     whole data-thread- prefix — rather than a spot check on one attribute.

     ONE <li> PER CARD WITH FLAT CHILDREN (I7): the acceptance probe slices a card from its opening <li>
     to the FIRST </li>, so anything list-shaped nested inside would truncate every later assertion
     against that card.

     data-feed-unread is an explicit STRING, because JTE drops a Boolean-valued attribute when false and
     "is not unread" would then pass on a card that had lost the hook altogether (§2.5). A post card is
     never unread: "N new" is about replies the owner has not read, and an opening is not one of them.

     data-feed-more discloses that the list is CUT rather than complete (§5, D7). There is no pagination
     and no cursor — adding one needs the whole-second stamp anomaly answered first — so saying so is the
     honest alternative. No scenario asserts this hook today (§11). --%>
<ul class="activity-stream" data-activity-stream data-feed-more="${(events.size >= FeedCards.STREAM_LIMIT).toString()}">
    @for(event in events)
        <li class="${if (event.unread) "activity-card is-unread" else "activity-card"}" data-feed-event="${event.id}" data-feed-kind="${event.kind}" data-feed-thread="${event.threadId}" data-feed-author="${event.author}" data-feed-unread="${event.unread.toString()}" data-nav-item="event" data-nav-id="${event.id}">
            <span class="monogram monogram--sm" aria-hidden="true" style="--mono-h: ${event.hue}">${event.monogram}</span>
            <span class="activity-card__byline">${event.byline}</span>
            <span class="activity-card__verb">${if (event.kind == "post") "opened" else "replied in"}</span>
            <a class="activity-card__thread" href="${event.threadHref}">${event.threadTitle}</a>
            <span class="activity-card__ago">${event.ago}</span>
            <a class="activity-card__open" href="${event.href}" aria-label="${if (event.kind == "post") "Open this post" else "Open this comment"}"></a>
            <span class="activity-card__excerpt">${event.excerpt}</span>
        </li>
    @endfor
</ul>
